imud (1.8.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: imud did not start on stock Debian. Every unit hardcoded
    Group=gpio, but nothing created the gpio or i2c groups; Raspberry Pi
    OS ships them and plain bookworm/trixie ships neither, so systemd
    refused to start the unit (216/GROUP). Both groups are now created if
    absent, on every install rather than only when the user is first
    created, so an upgrade repairs an affected host. New udev rule
    etc/60-imud.rules grants them /dev/i2c-* and /dev/gpiochip* access.
  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: the daemon and all five bridges now run with imud
    as their primary group, and the stream socket, /run/imud and
    /var/lib/imud are imud:imud. Only imud.service keeps gpio and i2c, as
    supplementary groups. Anything that read the stream socket or ran
    imud-status by virtue of gpio membership must join imud instead --
    on Pi OS that includes the default user: sudo adduser "$USER" imud.
  * Fix: config/imud-mqtt.conf (broker password) and
    config/imud-influxdb.conf (API token) installed mode 0644 despite
    carrying a SECURITY comment telling the operator to restrict them.
    Both are now 0640 root:imud, on upgrade over an existing 0644 file as
    well as on first install. The templates under
    /usr/share/doc/*/examples/ stay 0644.
  * Fix: a config that exists but cannot be read fell through to
    defaults, so a bridge exited reporting "disabled in config" for what
    was a permissions problem. EACCES is now distinct from ENOENT and
    fatal in the daemon and the bridges; a missing file still means
    defaults.
  * Fix: one configured ODR now means one rate everywhere. The filter was
    tuned from a round-to-nearest rate while every register-table driver
    programs the chip rounding up, so [imu] odr_hz = 900 tuned the MEKF
    for 833 Hz while the ISM330DHCX ran at 1660. The magnetometer rate
    was never snapped at all: [mag] odr_hz = 137 sized Rm for 137 Hz
    while the MMC5983MA sampled at 200. The driver is now the authority
    and the resolved rate reaches the chip, the filter and imud-imutest
    alike; startup logs "N Hz requested, M Hz actual" when they differ.
    Numerically unchanged with the shipped defaults, which are both
    already on their grids.
  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: odr_hz and the seven rate_hz keys now reject 0 and
    negative values. [mag] odr_hz = 0 gave Rm = 0 and a magnetometer
    Kalman gain of exactly 1. A config setting any of them non-positive
    started before and now refuses to start.
  * Fix: a client that connected to imud-prometheus and sent nothing
    stalled the bridge's single loop, stream reader included, for 2 s per
    iteration. The request is now read incrementally inside the loop's
    own poll and a quiet client is dropped at its deadline.
  * Fix: imud-imutest wrote its report to a file named "imud-im" when
    --report was not given.
  * Harden: tier-2 systemd sandboxing on all six units (empty
    CapabilityBoundingSet, @system-service syscall allow-list,
    RestrictNamespaces, LockPersonality, RestrictSUIDSGID,
    ProtectHostname, ProtectProc=invisible, ProcSubset=pid, UMask).
    imud.service deliberately omits ProtectClock= so the startup
    CLOCK_TAI check can call adjtimex(2) read-only. The AF_UNIX sockets
    are now born 0660 instead of being created wide and chmod'd after.
  * Harden: every fd is close-on-exec. Accepted sockets were the gap --
    POSIX does not carry FD_CLOEXEC across accept(), so NMEA/high-rate
    TCP clients, stream subscribers and imud-status connections were all
    inheritable on Linux.
  * Packaging: Architecture is now the little-endian release
    architectures (amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64) rather
    than any. The wire packet is a packed struct sent without byte-order
    conversion and the source #errors on a big-endian host, so any
    promised a build that cannot succeed.
  * Fix: make install DESTDIR=<root> captured config/cal.json into the
    packaging root when the build tree happened to have one, which made
    dpkg-buildpackage fail under dh_missing. A staged install now skips
    it; a real install is unchanged.
  * No wire-format change: the packet stays v17 / 276 bytes.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud (1.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New tool imud-imutest, shipped in the imud-utils binary package:
    validates a sensor driver against real hardware and writes a Markdown
    report to attach to an issue. imud-utils therefore gains a libgpiod
    dependency, since unlike imud-mon it talks to the sensor over I2C.
  * New drivers mpu9250 / mpu9255 (IMU) and ak8963 (magnetometer) for the
    TDK InvenSense MPU-925x 9-axis breakouts; all three experimental.
  * Fix: the IMU chip timer's declared period was trusted rather than
    measured. The reference ISM330DHCX runs 4.08% fast, so the wire's
    ts_wall_ns / ts_tai_ns ran roughly 2.4 s ahead over each 60 s anchor
    epoch and then stepped back, and every per-sample dt reaching the
    fusion filter was 4% long. The timestamp anchor now measures the
    counter's real period against CLOCK_MONOTONIC.
  * Fix: imud-cal accel printed the wrong physical instructions for all
    six positions and then silently fitted an identity scale. Re-run it.
  * Fix: imud-cal mag inflated the per-axis half-range by the hard-iron
    offset, biasing the soft-iron correction. Re-run it.
  * Files created by the daemon and tools now carry an explicit 0644
    instead of 0666 narrowed by the invoking process's umask.
  * No wire-format change: the packet stays v17 / 276 bytes.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 22:00:00 -0700

imud (1.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WIRE FORMAT v17 (packet 260 -> 276 bytes): four new MEKF diagnostic
    fields — innov_weight, innov_reject, nis_accel, nis_mag. The daemon,
    all five bridges and imud-mon validate the wire version and must be
    upgraded together; libimud consumers do not need recompiling.
  * Fusion: the MEKF error state grows 6 -> 9 with a Gauss-Markov
    wave-acceleration state, so the seaway's disturbance of the gravity
    measurement is modelled instead of treated as white sensor noise.
    New [fusion] keys mekf_wave_accel (0.8 m/s^2) and
    mekf_wave_accel_tau_s (0.5 s); either at 0 restores the 6-state
    filter exactly. New mekf_mag_dip_sigma_deg (1.0) admits the magnetic
    reference's dip uncertainty into the covariance in 3-D vector fusion.
  * Fusion: gross-outlier rejection widens 9x -> 25x the chi-squared
    gate, and the error-state reset Jacobian is applied to the covariance.
  * Fix: the innovation-covariance singularity test used an absolute
    determinant threshold on a matrix carrying physical units, silently
    skipping the accelerometer update once the filter converged.
  * Fix: initial attitude alignment averaged a hardcoded ~1 s of data, so
    a daemon started underway aligned to an arbitrary point in the wave
    cycle. The window is now [calibration] align_window_sec, default 5 s.
  * Fix: the update-gate health metrics used a per-sample averaging gain,
    giving a ~10 min time constant instead of 30 s; it is now time-based.
  * Config: the four MEKF noise densities are rejected at load if zero or
    negative; [mount] preset typos are fatal rather than silently applying
    a wrong rotation; new [mount] rotation_matrix key (9 row-major values,
    validated against R'R = I and det(R) = +1).
  * Engine-vibration detector: sample-rate-derived EMA time constant and
    threshold hysteresis so a boundary signal no longer chatters.
  * New imud-cal fit-ra mode reports the gravity-direction residual, its
    correlation time, the innovation distribution and the mean NIS from a
    rough-water capture.
  * imud-signalk: dest_addr now resolves hostnames and IPv6 via
    getaddrinfo(3) like every other bridge; unit gains AF_INET6.
  * imud-influxdb and imud-prometheus expose the four new diagnostics.
  * New test_fit_ra and test_mount suites; the wave benchmark averages
    over 12 seeds and the packet fuzz seed is generated from
    packet_build() with test_packet asserting it matches the wire.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud (1.6.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Internal dedup refactor, no functional change: the five bridges now
    share their startup/reload/main-loop scaffolding (src/bridge.c +
    src/sdnotify.c), all I2C drivers share the register-access helpers
    (src/drivers/i2c_io.h), and the WMM declination/field-reference
    derivation is a single shared function. Wire format, config keys,
    CLI, and log output are unchanged.
  * New test_bridge suite covers the shared bridge scaffolding.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud (1.6.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bridges: separate the daemon-level `enabled` from per-output enables.
    Stock configs now ship the daemon enabled but every output off
    (imud-signalk udp_enabled; imud-influxdb udp_enabled/http_enabled;
    imud-mqtt broker_enabled; imud-prometheus http_enabled; imud-mavlink
    unchanged). The daemon runs and stays healthy under systemd until an
    output is turned on.
  * BEHAVIOR CHANGE: imud-signalk UDP output is now gated by udp_enabled
    (previously always on when the bridge ran); add udp_enabled = true to
    existing configs to keep sending UDP.
  * imud-influxdb: `transport = "udp"|"http"` is deprecated in favour of
    udp_enabled/http_enabled (both may run at once); the old key is still
    honoured with a warning.
  * Fix: a bridge with enabled = false no longer crash-loops under systemd
    (Type=notify) — it signals readiness before exiting cleanly.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud (1.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TCP outputs for NMEA, the framed binary stream, Signal K, and MAVLink
    (per-output tcp_enabled/tcp_bind_addr/tcp_port keys); libimud gains
    imud_connect_tcp (additive, SONAME unchanged).
  * BEHAVIOR CHANGE: built-in defaults now enable only the local AF_UNIX
    stream socket (NMEA UDP default flipped to off); set [nmea]
    enabled = true to restore the old posture.

